# React

- Presentational components take props and return JSX. No hooks that fetch, no module-level stores.
- Containers own state and call hooks. They render a presentational child. Do not mix both in one file.
- Derive values during render. An effect that only copies props into state is a bug.
- Name handlers `handleX`. Pass a stable function, not an inline arrow, when the child is memoized.
- Conditional UI is an early return or a named element. Do not nest ternaries.
- Loading, empty, and error each have a visible state. A spinner is not the empty state.
- Extract a hook when the same stateful logic is used by two components. One `useState` stays inline.
- Split a component when it has two reasons to change, not when it merely feels long.

